<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	Athina's entitlements, for the development bundle (scripts/bundle.sh) and the
	direct-download release (scripts/release.sh) alike. Keep it to what the app
	does today, each key with the reason it is here.

	The release runs under the hardened runtime, which Developer ID notarization
	requires. Nothing else Athina does needs an exception to it: screen capture,
	Accessibility, and the microphone are privacy permissions the person grants,
	not entitlements, and every speech recognizer runs on this Mac without the
	system's Speech Recognition permission; the Carbon hotkey, the login
	keychain, the network (no App Sandbox), Vision, and the SQLite shim linked
	into the binary need none; and the release signs the library the app
	embeds, whisper.cpp, which runs the Whisper and Parakeet speech models, with
	the app's own team, so library validation passes without disabling it. No
	JIT, no unsigned executable memory, no Apple Events.

	The App Sandbox is off. An App Store variant starts from a copy of this file
	that adds com.apple.security.app-sandbox and the sandbox entitlements the app
	then needs, such as com.apple.security.network.client; the microphone key
	below serves the sandbox as well, and nothing here needs to change for it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
		The talk-back shortcut listens through AVAudioEngine. The hardened runtime
		refuses microphone input without this, whatever the person granted in
		System Settings. The unhardened development build does not need it.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
